course: dictionary
lesson: 13525
title: Bossy and proud: imperiously
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Imperiously is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something. It means in a proud, bossy way, as if they expect to be obeyed at once. «"Bring me my crown now!" said the queen imperiously.» The word tells you how she spoke, not only what she said.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Who is speaking, and what do they want? A king, a queen, or a captain giving orders is a good sign. «The captain pointed imperiously at the deck, and the crew ran to obey.» The crew running at once shows that the order was obeyed quickly.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a simple word, such as bossily, and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you are right. The word sounds a bit like emperor, a ruler with great power, which can help you remember that it is about being in charge.
fact: Imperiously means in a proud, bossy way, expecting to be obeyed at once.
fact: «Imperiously» is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does an action.
fact: The Queen of Hearts in Alice in Wonderland speaks imperiously all the time.
fact: Toad orders people about imperiously when he feels grand.
fact: Imperiously shows arrogance and power: the speaker thinks they are the boss.
exercise: «"Fetch my crown at once!" the queen commanded imperiously.» What does imperiously mean here? | In a shy, quiet way with eyes down | In a sleepy way, yawning | *In a proud, bossy way | In a happy, singing way
exercise: «Toad waved his paw imperiously, and the servants rushed to fetch his carriage.» Find and copy the word that tells you how Toad waved. | paw | carriage | *imperiously | Toad
exercise: «The teacher said imperiously, "Sit down."» Which feeling does imperiously show? | Being very scared | Being sleepy | *Being sure you are in charge | Being sorry
test: «"Stop talking and listen," the captain said imperiously.» What is the captain like? | A kind nurse at a hospital | A scared mouse under a chair | A shy child lost in a shop | *A bossy leader who expects to be obeyed
test: Which sentence shows the meaning of imperiously best? | The girl hid behind her mum and whispered sorry. | *The king clicked his fingers, and his guards came running at once. | The rain fell softly on the roof. | The dog wagged its tail and sat down quietly.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to imperiously? | gently | nervously | *bossily | sleepily
